## Implementation

At executor entry, a real `SystemOptimizationActivitySnapshot` from the transaction engine must be Idle. Through before capture and before comparison evidence/mutation, generation must remain unchanged. The canary's own successful `BeginSessionAsync` is recognized narrowly as exactly one completed operation: Idle before and after, no active operations, generation delta exactly +2. Any overlapping or additional engine operation makes that proof fail.

After the canary mutation, the exact post-own-operation snapshot becomes the new baseline. It must remain uninterrupted through after capture, comparison evidence and evaluator. Any process-local DG System Optimization operation in those stages invokes exact session restore and returns Inconclusive/no active lease/KEEP. The TEST evidence deliberately supplies `OtherMutationDetected=false`; Core activity remains authoritative.

## Limits and exact continuation

This is observation/detection, not mutual exclusion. A race remains after final reads, and operations outside the DG process (Regedit, vendor/driver tools, other software) are not covered. Scene/mode/load/environment provenance also remains absent in production; FF/FF MAX explicitly have `CanaryContextEvidence=false`.

Next bounded TDD is an owner-managed generic session lifecycle boundary: own the exact OS session epoch and every retained canary lease, restore every lease before coordinator Reset/rebind/disposal, and never orphan a kept mutation. After that, introduce true host-level exclusion/coordination with Track0 controlled benchmarks and DG System Optimization plus specialized Guardian suspend/reconcile. Generic automatic activation and real-game HIL remain blocked. Track6 item3 remains IN PROGRESS; item4 reliability and item5 post-session queue remain pending.

This documentary commit itself requires a fresh exact-head Windows CI before being marked GREEN.
